    delphi:hasScore "0.722"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The anatomical trajectory and expression count are standard measurable outcomes, and public expression archives are plausible direct resources. They test the narrow experimental result well but not the stronger claim of purposive navigation or absence of relevant prior selection." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Analyze survival, head loss and regrowth under barium together with differential expression before and after adaptation, using preregistered thresholds for the number and magnitude of changed genes. Compare with untreated and acute-stress controls to identify changes associated specifically with restored morphology." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "'Handful' depends on statistical thresholds and sampling time.", "Expression changes may miss protein and physiological regulation.", "No prior selection for barium is a historical inference." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2023-agential-15--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2023-agential-15--gpt--dataset-2> .
